<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Milner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lord Milner, Viscount Milner</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Milner was a British colonial administrator who as high commissioner for southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from 1897 pressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. After the war he governed the Transvaal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> Colonies until 1905, rebuilding their administration and gold industry with a group of young officials known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milners-kindergarten">Milner's Kindergarten</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-milner.jpg" alt="Alfred Milner" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elliott &amp;amp; Fry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lord_Milner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
